PROVED (S5.1): every E-cycle other than (1,4,2) uses >= 1 even->3n+1 arrow: a cycle avoiding
  them is a cycle of the deterministic Collatz map, whose only cycle on nodes <= 2000 is (1,4,2)
  (FINITE-EXACT input from S3, n <= 10^6; the published verification bound n < 2^68 is
   UNCITED-RECOLLECTION (Barina, J. Supercomputing 2021, from memory) and is NOT used anywhere).
  Every E-cycle has 2^h > 3^a (positivity of n = B/(2^h-3^a)); the lengths observed are
  exactly a+h with 2^h > 3^a > 2^(h-1)... see the note.  The user's 16-cycle through 2->7 is #1 of len 16.

